      "why": "Meets throughput (1 result/cycle) and is the area-optimal way to get 1/cycle throughput: it registers every m stages, drastically cutting FFs vs full pipelined while keeping the 1/cycle schedule. m=2..4 balances the FF count against the critical path (Fmax) needed to hold >=1 MSPS. W=12..18 and N=10..16 cover the accuracy requirement (err <= 2^-10) with margin to explore the accuracy_bits objective."
