      ],
      "budget_share": 0.35,
      "why": "The reference 1/cycle architecture. It has the most FFs (one register per stage) but the shortest per-stage critical path, so it is the safe anchor for the throughput constraint and the high-Fmax / high-accuracy corner of the front. Comparing it against pipelined_m lets the search find where the FF savings of m-staging start to hurt Fmax."
